2026-09-27T01:50:40Z table diplotypes.csv rows='All 6 rows kept with unchanged gene, haplotype pair, phenotype label, trait_efo_id and direction; the conclusion cell rewritten on 6 of 6 rows.' (source literature review (11 PMIDs in studies.csv); Version 1.1.0: every factual claim in the conclusions checked against papers found and title-verified in this session. Changed where sources disagreed: e3/e4 frequency 1 in 5 -> about 1 in 4 and ε2/ε4 2 -> 2 to 3 in 100 (UK Biobank, PMID 32818802); e3/e4 'two to three times' and e4/e4 'several times' replaced by lifetime risks by age 85 (PMID 21556001) with ancestry differences (PMIDs 37930705, 9343467); e2/e4 'studies disagree' replaced by the consistent moderate raise found in European-ancestry studies; e2/e3 'modest' replaced by sourced size and ancestry limits; e2/e2 dysbetalipoproteinaemia 'small share' replaced by 1 in 10 to 1 in 3 (PMIDs 35781703, 38625929) and 'a standard cholesterol test would show it' made precise; e4/e4 earlier onset sourced (PMIDs 38710950, 8346443); practical note on anti-amyloid antibody side-effect risk added for e4 carriers (PMID 37357276). Rewritten in the module-voice form.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false
2026-09-27T01:50:40Z table studies.csv rows='New table: 11 rows, one per claim-supporting paper, no variant key (the claims are about allele pairs, not one site). 9 rows carry a verbatim provenance_quote located in fetch_fulltext output (5 of them from abstracts); 2 rows (CC BY-NC-ND articles) carry none on purpose.' (source PubMed / Europe PMC via literature_search and fetch_fulltext; Grounds every claim in the 1.1.0 conclusions. PMIDs taken from literature_search results in this session with titles checked; population and design from each paper's methods or, where only the abstract was retrievable, from the abstract; doi left empty per find-evidence; curator names the agent that located the quotes.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false
2026-09-27T01:50:40Z table licensing.csv rows="New table: 15 rows. 1 annotation row for the module's own tables (MIT); 9 annotation rows for articles whose text is quoted (3 CC-BY, 6 with terms unknown and flags left blank); 2 literature rows for CC BY-NC-ND articles cited without text; 3 literature rows for pubmed, europepmc and unpaywall." (source Unpaywall via lookup_open_access, per article; Per-article terms from lookup_open_access; blank means unknown, never false. NC-ND articles kept at the literature layer with no text carried so the declared MIT licence is not contradicted.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false
