2026-09-27T08:01:58Z table diplotypes.csv rows="All six conclusions revised after two independent AI reviews: Genin lifetime risks reworded as modelled estimates for people who live to 85; e4/e4 gives the range about half to two in three plus near-full AD biology (Fortea) instead of '4 in 10 had not developed it'; 'When symptoms come' -> 'If symptoms do come'; e2/e4 'a little less than one e4 with one e3 does' -> 'less than one e4 and one e3 do', 'likely rather than certain' -> 'less certain than the others, because fewer people with this combination have been studied', e1/e3 caveat as last sentence; e3/e3 baseline most people share; epsilon and APOE2/3/4 explained in each; antibody medicines glossed; e2/e2 blood-fat disorder named plainly first, triglycerides -> another blood fat; risk results say APOE is not used to predict AD in people without symptoms. Labels, pairs and directions unchanged." (source review findings (lay reader and scientific reviewer); PMIDs 21556001 and 38710950 read this session; Reconciling the two independent reviews; changed numbers checked against Genin 2011 PMC author manuscript (CIs 41-70 and 47-84, PAQUID 68%) and the Fortea 2024 abstract (near-full penetrance of AD biology).) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false [replaced an earlier record]
2026-09-27T08:01:58Z table studies.csv rows='PMID 21556001 summary: lifetime risks labelled modelled and conditional on surviving to 85, e4/e4 CIs and PAQUID 68% added. PMID 38710950 summary: near-full penetrance of AD biology added. Quotes unchanged.' (source PMID 21556001 (PMC3162068) and PMID 38710950 abstract via fetch_fulltext; Keep study summaries consistent with the revised conclusions.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false [replaced an earlier record]
2026-09-27T08:02:20Z table diplotypes.csv rows="Version 1.1.0 conclusions. (1) Rewrite: every factual claim checked against papers found and title-verified in the curating session (11 PMIDs in studies.csv): UK Biobank frequencies (32818802), lifetime risks by 85 (21556001) with ancestry differences (37930705, 9343467), e2/e2 dysbetalipoproteinaemia 1 in 10 to 1 in 3 (35781703, 38625929), e4/e4 earlier onset (38710950, 8346443), anti-amyloid antibody side-effect note (37357276); module-voice form. (2) Revision after two independent AI reviews (2026-09-27): lifetime risks worded as modelled estimates for people who live to 85; e4/e4 range about half to two in three plus near-full AD biology (Fortea) instead of '4 in 10 had not developed it'; 'When symptoms come' -> 'If symptoms do come'; e2/e4 'a little less than one e4 with one e3 does' -> 'less than one e4 and one e3 do', 'likely rather than certain' -> 'less certain than the others, because fewer people with this combination have been studied', e1/e3 caveat last; e3/e3 baseline most people share; epsilon and APOE2/3/4 explained in each; antibody medicines glossed; e2/e2 blood-fat disorder named plainly first, triglycerides -> another blood fat; risk results say APOE is not used to predict AD in people without symptoms. Labels, pairs and directions unchanged." (source literature review (11 PMIDs in studies.csv) and review findings (lay reader, scientific reviewer); Reconciling the two independent reviews on top of the 1.1.0 rewrite; changed numbers checked against Genin 2011 PMC author manuscript (CIs 41-70 and 47-84, PAQUID 68%) and the Fortea 2024 abstract.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false [replaced an earlier record]
